<Base title="Our story" description="Why Faraway Foods exists: exploring great food should be open to everyone.">
  <h1>Great food shouldn’t be for a few.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Exploring exotic food should be open to everyone, not just people who travel often or know the right importer.</p>
  <p>In India, the real thing is often hard to find or priced for a small circle: ceremonial matcha, aged soy sauce, a proper parmesan. What reaches most shelves is a substitute.</p>
  <p>Faraway Foods brings it in the way that keeps prices fair. We pick one country, work with makers directly, and import only what is pre-ordered. No unsold stock to price in, and the savings go to you.</p>
  <p>We start with shelf-stable pantry foods from Japan, then follow your requests to the next country.</p>
  <p><a href="/drops/">See our drops</a></p>
</Base>
